  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "V.Krishnappa vs John @ John Rogert on 14 October, 2025 Kabc0C0345812018 Presented on : 20-12-2018 Registered on : 20-12-2018 Decided on : 14-10-2025 Duration : 6 years, 9 months, 25 days In The Court Of The Xxix Addl.C.J.M Mayohall Unit, Bengaluru -: Present :- Sri. Girish Chatni, B.A., LL.B(Spl) Xxix Addl. Chief Judicial Magistrate, Bengaluru. Dated: This the 14th Day of October, 2025 Criminal Case No.60156/2018 The State by Kothanuru Police Station. ... Complainant. (By Learned Assistant Public Prosecutor) // Versus // John @ John Robert, S/o Late. Rayappa, Aged about 48 years, R/at: No.51, Bairathi Village, 5th Cross, Kothanuru Post, 2 C.C.No.60156/2018 Bengaluru - 560077. ... Accused (By Sri.K.V.S.R, Advocate) Date of commission of offence : 25.01.2018 Date of report of offence : 25.01.2018 V.Krishnappa vs John @ John Rogert on 14 October, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/100274497/ 1",
    "facts": "2. BRIEF FACTS OF THE PROSECUTION CASE ARE AS UNDER : It is the case of the complainant that, on 25.01.2018 at 7.00 AM, the accused has negligently left his dogs on Ayyappa Temple Road, Bairathi Village, to which they have all of sudden attacked CW.1, when he tried to escape, the said dogs followed CW.1 and harassed him. It is further alleged that, accused came to the spot and when CW.1 enquired with him stating that, he should not leave the said dogs negligently on the road, to which the accused talked with CW.1 in high voice and also threatened with dire consequences. Based on the typed complaint lodged by C.W.1, C.W.7 registered the case against accused in P.S. Crime No.14/2018 for the offence punishable under sections 506, 289 of IPC. Investigating Officer/CW.7 investigated the matter, after completion of the investigation, has submitted final report against the accused for Offence punishable U/Secs. 289, 506 of IPC. C.C.No.60156/2018 3 . Upon receipt of charge sheet, cognizance was taken for the above said offences alleged against the accused and registered the criminal case against him. 4. After registering the case, the accused has appeared and was enlarged on bail. Copy of the charge sheet and its' enclosures were furnished to the accused in compliance of section 207 of Cr.P.C. Sufficient grounds were made out to frame charges. Hence, charges framed and read over to the accused. He pleaded not guilty and claimed to be tried. 5. In order to prove the guilt of the accused, the prosecution has examined 03 witnesses out of 07 witnesses cited in the charge sheet as P.W.1 to P.W.3 and got marked 04 documents as per Ex.P.1 to V.Krishnappa vs John @ John Rogert on 14 October, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/100274497/ 2 Ex.P.4 and closed its side. Thereafter, the accused was examined as provided U/s 313 of Cr.P.C by explaining incriminating evidence appearing against him. The accused has denied the same and has not produced any oral or documentary evidence. 6. Heard both sides. In order to prove the above said allegations, the prosecution has examined the complainant/ victim/ CW.1 as PW.1, wherein, he has supported the case of the prosecution and deposed that, on 25.01.2018 at 7.00 PM, he was coming back from walking at Ayyappa Temple Road of Bairathi Vil- lage, Two dogs followed him, he tried to escape, however, the said dogs barked at him and all of sudden attacked CW.1, to which he sustained scratched injuries on hand, legs and on body. He has further deposed that, a person came over there C.C.No.60156/2018 and on enquiry he submitted that, he is the owner of the dogs and also threatened him with dire consequences. PW.1 has further deposed that, by 1.00 PM, on the said day, he lodged complaint and the police authorities have conducted spot mahazar in his presence. 11. The prosecution has examined the independent witnesses i.e., CW.5 and 6 as PW.2 and 3, wherein, they have partly supported the case of the prosecution and they have de- posed that, at 7.00 AM, they were coming back from walking at Ayyappa Temple road, CW.1 was attacked by the Dogs of the accused and CW.1 was taken to the hospital.",
    "arguments": "13. The essential ingredients in order to constitute an offence U/s 289 of IPC are as follows; i) The offence involves an animal. ii) The accused must have acted negligently with respect to the animal. iii) The negligent conduct must be likely to cause harm or injury to any person.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "13. The essential ingredients in order to constitute an offence U/s 289 of IPC are as follows; i) The offence involves an animal. ii) The accused must have acted negligently with respect to the animal. iii) The negligent conduct must be likely to cause harm or injury to any person."
  },
